> is decidedly worse than TikZ is access to font info.  With TIkZ we can
> extract all sorts of useful information such as the ascent and descent of
> characters. With MetaPost, the only clear parameter that can be clearly
> extracted is the overall height of the text box.  So, text may not
> vertically center exactly as it should---but things like legends will at
> least look passable.
>

I just pushed an update that enables proper font metric calculation with
both ascent and descent being returned. Also, I found that MetaPost has
an inherent "label offset" that was causing text to be placed a short
distance away from where R wanted it to be.  I turned this off so legend
titles should no longer be smashed up against the top of their boxes and
text should be vertically centered.  Things are still slightly off as I
cannot find a good way in MetaPost to anchor strings at their baselines
rather than the bottom of their bounding boxes.

If you have a permanent metrics dictionary, you will need to delete it so
that the tikzDevice will re-calculate these new values.

-Charlie

